\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{A source coefficient at a zero kernel}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{For #{V=k} and the scalar kernel #{K=c}, the
[ring source polynomial](fdip-00TN) is
##{\mathscr Z_c=c+\bar\eta\eta.}
Indeed the field top word is #{\psi\bar\psi}. It is selected
either from #{c\psi\bar\psi} or from
#{(\bar\eta\psi)(\bar\psi\eta)
 =\bar\eta\eta\psi\bar\psi}. Thus the coefficient of
#{\bar\eta\eta} is one even when #{c=0}. A vanishing
partition coefficient need not erase inserted coefficients.}
